-- title:
--   A fibre model forces the residue map to be surjective
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a prime $\ell$, a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$. Write $L$ for `laurentBaseChange` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ along `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, i.e. the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the elements of the field $\mathbb{Q}(\text{divisorExpansions } N)$, and let $\bar{j}, \bar{j}_N \in L$ be the images of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j(q^N)$. Assume given a term of `FibreModel N A ℓ k red`: two subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of $L$, each containing the image of $A$ under the constants homomorphism $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to L$, with $\bar{j}, \bar{j}_N \in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar{j}^{-1} \in B_{\mathrm{inf}}$, each integral over the subring generated by the constants together with $\bar{j}$, respectively $\bar{j}^{-1}$, and ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}} : B_{\mathrm{fin}} \to F$, $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}} : B_{\mathrm{inf}} \to F$ to $F = k(\text{jqModC } k, \text{jqNModC } k\, N) \subseteq k((q))$ carrying the constant $a$ to $\mathrm{red}(a)$ and $\bar{j}, \bar{j}_N, \bar{j}^{-1}$ to the corresponding characteristic-$\ell$ $q$-expansions, together with the remaining data and compatibility axioms of the structure, summarised here. The conclusion is that $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ is surjective.
--
--   The fibre-model structure does not postulate that $k$ be the residue field of $A$; this lemma shows that it is forced, the reduction data of the two charts pinning the image of $\mathrm{red}$ down to all of $k$. It is used in the identification of $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with coefficientwise reduction and in the two statements that the ranges of $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ localise to the affine charts of the characteristic-$\ell$ model.
